  "status": "Application Under Consideration",
  "description": "The proposal is to replace the existing rear-facing single-glazed timber windows with new timber double-glazed windows designed as an exact like-for-like match to the original historic windows in terms of proportions, joinery detailing, glazing bar thickness, horn profiles, opening method and positioning within the brickwork reveal.\n\nThe existing windows are in poor condition and no longer perform adequately in terms of thermal efficiency or security. Replacement is therefore required to improve the performance of the building while retaining its historic character.\n\nThe new windows will be manufactured in painted timber and will replicate the traditional design and detailing of the originals. Slim-profile double glazed units will be used to enhance thermal and acoustic performance while maintaining the external appearance. The works are limited to the rear elevation only and will not affect the front elevation.\n\nIn addition, the existing front entrance door will be replaced with a new painted timber door designed to match the traditional character and detailing of the original door. The replacement door will incorporate improved thermal performance and enhanced security, including upgraded locking mechanisms, while retaining traditional joinery features and appearance.\n\nOverall, the proposed works are intended to improve the thermal performance and security of the property while preserving the architectural character of the building and the Hyde Farm Conservation Area.",
